# config/nav-orphans.allow
#
# EN docs pages intentionally not linked from the sidebar (config/sidebar.mjs).
# Format: one slug per line with a trailing "# reason" comment (required).
# bin/check-orphans.mjs fails on unlisted orphans AND on stale entries here
# (slug now linked from the sidebar, or page deleted).
#
# The list is EMPTY, and that is the intended state: after the Phase 2
# information-architecture rework every EN page is reachable from the sidebar.
# The seven entries this file used to carry were all retired by that rework —
# docs-overview was deleted outright; pricing gained a sidebar link under
# Plans & billing; and the five translations/universal/* children, previously
# reachable only from their index page's body, are now linked from the
# Translations & contributing group. None of them was an intentional orphan on
# the merits: each was a page the sidebar could not file, not a page the
# sidebar chose not to file.
#
# Add an entry only for a page that is genuinely meant to be reachable by URL
# alone — and say why in the reason, because the reason is the only thing
# stopping the entry from becoming a place to park navigation debt.
